@startuml

title Starting a feed: the command, the consent and the run token

hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

actor "Operator" as op
participant "Synthetic service" as syn
participant "IAM" as iam
participant "Marketdata" as md

op -> syn : synthetic.v1.ops.start_feed(config id)\nAuthorization: the operator's token
syn -> syn : check the operator's permissions\n(the kind's config permission and the run permission)

alt the collection holds no run grant
    syn -> iam : iam.v1.run_grants.put(resource, role, audience)\nthe operator's token, relayed
    iam -> iam : check the operator holds every permission\nof the role in the collection's party
    iam --> syn : grant id
    syn -> syn : record the grant id on the collection
end

syn -> iam : iam.v1.ops.exchange_run_grant(grant id, run id)\nAuthorization: the service's own token
iam -> iam : check the audience, the grant, the tenant and the grantor\npermissions = the role's, limited to the grantor's now
iam --> syn : run token (five minutes)

syn -> md : read the vintage series and observations\nAuthorization: the run token
syn -> syn : start the feed
syn -> md : create the operator's feed binding if absent\nAuthorization: the operator's token

syn --> op : started

note over syn
    The operator's token serves the permission check,
    the consent and the operator's own binding.
    The feed itself does not depend on who pressed Start.
end note

@enduml
